.com/en/south-korea-s-gender-pay-gap-grows-as-women-get-older/a-79431285?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report shows how in South Korea, women on average earn less and have fewer employment opportunities throughout their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48601a0841cb6a0ed9185cbeccf6bcf0351c2e8e14ea6f0e8014f4319fa9e430</id><updated>2026-10-02T20:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
